Z||000007||reddog||10-25-2001||11:54 AM||||Ok I can't tell you much about the material. The only thing I do Know is that the seats are made of injection molded foam. The material Looks to be some kind of synthetic blend(Is extremely soft to touch) High wear patches are leather( or maybe Pleather ). They are very comfortable and give excellent support. It didn't take any mods to mount them Corbeau makes mounting brackets for the fiero. The seats slide back as far as stock.However they will not recline as far back as the stock buckets, due to their design the shoulders overlap the center console a little and if pushed all the way back and reclined the seat will make contact and rub during driving causing an annoying little squeak! I don't have this problem because I am "Vertically Challenged" and have trouble reaching the pedals comfortably from the back position.(5'7" tall) But from the back of the seat to the front of the first firewall is still only about 1 1/2- 2" Also the seat sits just a tiny bit higher than stock but I like it that way.Anyone over 6' may not feel the same way. As far as pricing goes I paid about $950. for both seats and the mounting brackets but I sure you can probably find them cheaper somewhere.<BR>For more info on the seats go <A HREF="http://www.corbeau.com/brochure/carrera.html" TARGET=_blank>www.corbeau.com/brochure/carrera.html</A> <BR>;p ;p<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000008||reddog||10-25-2001||11:56 AM||||And yes, I REALLY LOVE THEM!!!!!!!!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
